    id: "20260915-12296",
    trackers: ["os"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Xfce 桌面環境客製化指南：修復 macOS/Unity 佈局及優化 Dock 功能",
    summary: "本文為 Xfce 桌面環境的進階客製化教學，旨在優化其 Panel Profiles 工具所支援的 macOS（Cupertino）和 Unity 佈局。文章指出，預設的佈局在細節上存在瑕疵，例如 Unity 佈局的狀態圖示位置不當，以及 macOS 佈局的菜單對齊問題。修復方法包括：在 Panel Preferences 的 Items 標籤中，為 Unity 佈局添加一個透明且可擴展的分隔符（Separator），將狀態圖示推至右側；對於 Cupertino 佈局，只需在 AppMenu plugin 的設定中取消勾選「Expand」即可修正菜單對齊。此外，文章推薦使用「Docklike Taskbar」插件取代預設的「Window Buttons」，以實現更高效能的 Dock 功能，結合了應用程式啟動器和運行應用程式指示器。這類客製化操作主要透過 Xfce 的 Panel Preferences 進行，對於希望達到更接近原生系統體驗的用戶具有實用價值。",
    tags: ["Xfce", "Linux", "Panel Profiles", "Docklike Taskbar", "macOS", "Unity"],
    title_en: "Xfce Desktop Environment Customization Guide: Fixing macOS/Unity Layouts and Optimizing Dock Functionality",
    summary_en: "This article provides an advanced customization tutorial for the Xfce desktop environment, aiming to optimize the macOS (Cupertino) and Unity layouts supported by the Panel Profiles tool. It points out that the default layouts have minor flaws, such as the incorrect positioning of status icons in the Unity layout, and menu alignment issues in the macOS layout. Methods for fixing these include: adding a transparent and expandable Separator in the Items tab of Panel Preferences for the Unity layout, pushing the status icons to the right; and for the Cupertino layout, simply unchecking 'Expand' in the AppMenu plugin settings to correct the menu alignment. Furthermore, the article recommends using the 'Docklike Taskbar' plugin to replace the default 'Window Buttons' plugin, achieving more efficient Dock functionality that combines an application launcher and a running application indicator. These customization operations are primarily performed through Xfce's Panel Preferences and are valuable for users seeking an experience closer to native operating systems.",
    tags_en: ["Xfce", "Linux", "Panel Profiles", "Docklike Taskbar", "macOS", "Unity"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Register", url: "https://theregister.com/software/2026/09/15/give-xfce-a-mac-or-unity-style-makeover/5295937", lang: "EN" }
    ]
