    category: "法規與標準",
    title: "微軟與教師工會簽署AI教育安全協議：限制學生數據用於訓練，確立產業標準",
    summary: "隨著AI聊天機器人日益普及，教育界對於學生數據隱私和AI使用規範的擔憂日益增加。美國兩大學區（紐約市、洛杉磯）已暫停學生使用AI，促使微軟（Microsoft）與美國教師聯合會（AFT）達成協議。該協議要求微軟不得使用學生或教育工作者的數據來訓練AI系統，除非是為了保護學生。此外，協議還禁止使用任何旨在建立情感依賴或讓學生過度沉迷的AI功能。微軟承諾將在所有簽約學校實施這些標準，並要求第三方審計以確保合規性。雖然OpenAI和Anthropic等公司也表示正在與AFT討論類似的協議，但Google等主要教育科技供應商是否會跟進，仍是業界關注的焦點。此協議被視為在缺乏聯邦和州級立法的情況下，為學區設定的產業高標準。",
    tags: ["Microsoft", "AFT", "AI 隱私", "教育科技", "數據隱私", "產業標準"],
    title_en: "Microsoft and Teachers Union Sign AI Education Safety Agreement: Restricting Student Data Use for Training, Establishing Industry Standard",
    summary_en: "As AI chatbots become increasingly prevalent, concerns regarding student data privacy and AI usage guidelines are growing within the education sector. Two US school districts (New York City and Los Angeles) have temporarily suspended student use of AI, prompting Microsoft to reach an agreement with the American Federation of Teachers (AFT). The agreement stipulates that Microsoft cannot use student or educator data to train its AI systems, unless it is for the purpose of student protection. Furthermore, the agreement prohibits the use of any AI features designed to create emotional dependency or excessive student addiction. Microsoft has committed to implementing these standards in all signatory schools and requires third-party audits to ensure compliance. Although companies like OpenAI and Anthropic have also indicated discussions with the AFT regarding similar agreements, whether major EdTech suppliers like Google will follow suit remains a key focus for the industry. This agreement is viewed as setting a high industry standard for school districts in the absence of federal and state legislation.",
    tags_en: ["Microsoft", "AFT", "AI Privacy", "EdTech", "Data Privacy", "Industry Standard"],
    sources: [
      { name: "SecurityWeek", url: "https://securityweek.com/microsoft-commits-to-sweeping-ai-privacy-rules-for-students-will-other-tech-giants-follow", lang: "EN" }
    ]
