    title: "Windows 11 家庭版用戶可透過 OOBE 繞過強制使用 Microsoft 帳號的限制",
    summary: "本文介紹了一種針對 Windows 11 家庭版（Home Edition）的設定繞過方法。在系統的開機體驗（OOBE）過程中，當系統提示用戶需要使用 Microsoft 帳號時，用戶只需點擊「Learn more」連結，即可跳過帳號驗證步驟，直接進入要求輸入用戶名稱和密碼的介面。這讓用戶可以在不綁定 Microsoft 帳號的情況下完成作業系統的初始設定。雖然 Microsoft 過去曾多次修補類似的漏洞，但此方法提供了一個簡單的點擊操作來避免強制使用 Microsoft 帳號。此繞過方法僅適用於 Windows 11 家庭版，而 Windows 11 Pro 或專業版用戶則有其他選項，因此該漏洞可能存在於設計層面。文章提醒，由於 Microsoft 傾向將用戶導向其線上生態系統，此漏洞可能很快就會被修補。",
    tags: ["Windows 11", "Home Edition", "OOBE", "Microsoft 帳號", "系統設定", "Windows 漏洞"],
    title_en: "Windows 11 Home Edition Users Can Bypass Mandatory Microsoft Account Requirement via OOBE",
    summary_en: "This article introduces a configuration bypass method targeting Windows 11 Home Edition. During the Out-of-Box Experience (OOBE) process, when the system prompts the user to use a Microsoft account, the user can simply click the \"Learn more\" link to skip the account verification step and proceed directly to the interface that requires entering a username and password. This allows users to complete the operating system's initial setup without linking a Microsoft account. Although Microsoft has previously patched similar vulnerabilities multiple times, this method provides a simple click operation to avoid the mandatory use of a Microsoft account. This bypass method is only applicable to Windows 11 Home Edition; users of Windows 11 Pro or Professional editions have other options, suggesting the vulnerability may exist at a design level. The article cautions that because Microsoft tends to guide users toward its online ecosystem, this vulnerability may be patched soon.",
