    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "美國、英國、荷蘭警告：伊朗情報部門利用 Telegram 惡意軟體監控反對派與記者",
    summary: "美國聯邦調查局（FBI）、英國國家網路安全中心（NCSC）和荷蘭情報部門（AIVD）聯合發布警告，揭露一種由伊朗情報部門（MOIS）使用的 Windows 惡意軟體。該惡意軟體被稱為 HEAVYGRAM 或 CHOSEN BRICK，可透過 Telegram 訊息應用程式傳播和控制。攻擊者透過偽裝成已知聯絡人或技術支援來誘騙目標點擊惡意檔案，該檔案會在背景安裝惡意軟體。一旦感染，惡意軟體能竊取目標的電子郵件、聊天記錄、截圖，並啟動麥克風錄音。它還能存取儲存的密碼、電子郵件地址，並可透過 Telegram bot 或 Vultr、Storj 等雲端服務將資料外傳。受害者包括伊朗的異議人士、反伊朗記者和活動家，資料外洩甚至可能增加其人身安全風險。為防範，建議使用者勿點擊來源不明的連結或開啟訊息中的檔案，並保持作業系統和應用程式的更新。網路管理員應啟用防釣魚型多因素驗證，並監控系統登錄檔的異常變動（如 Run key）和可疑的網路連線。",
    tags: ["Iran MOIS", "HEAVYGRAM", "CHOSEN BRICK", "Telegram", "Windows malware", "情報戰", "網路監控"],
    title_en: "US, UK, Netherlands Warn: Iranian Intelligence Uses Telegram Malware to Monitor Dissidents and Journalists",
    summary_en: "The FBI, UK's National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC), and the Netherlands' AIVD jointly issued a warning about a Windows malware used by Iranian intelligence (MOIS). This malware, known as HEAVYGRAM or CHOSEN BRICK, can spread and be controlled through the Telegram messaging application. Attackers trick targets into clicking malicious files by impersonating known contacts or technical support. Once infected, the malware can steal the target's emails, chat logs, and screenshots, and activate the microphone for recording. It can also access stored passwords and email addresses, and exfiltrate data via Telegram bots or cloud services like Vultr and Storj. Victims include Iranian dissidents, anti-Iran journalists, and activists, and the leaked data could even increase their physical safety risks. To prevent infection, users are advised not to click on unknown links or open files received in messages, and to keep their operating systems and applications updated. Network administrators should enable anti-phishing multi-factor authentication and monitor for abnormal changes in system registry entries (such as the Run key) and suspicious network connections.",
    tags_en: ["Iran MOIS", "HEAVYGRAM", "CHOSEN BRICK", "Telegram", "Windows malware", "Information Warfare", "Network Surveillance"],
