    summary_en: "According to analyst Jeff Pu's report, Apple's newly launched iPhone Duo (a foldable phone) is expected to face significant supply challenges. The report indicates that production slowdowns due to 'hinge constraints' will reduce the estimated shipment volume of the iPhone Duo in 2026 to 6 million units, falling below previous estimates. Although pre-orders for the iPhone Duo open on October 16th, with the first delivery date set for October 23rd, the analyst warns that even reaching a sales volume of 6 million units, its market share in the overall iPhone market (approximately 6–9%) still represents a significant gap compared to the current market share of foldable phones in the non-Apple smartphone market (approximately 2–3%). This suggests that consumers may face extreme difficulty acquiring the high-priced iPhone Duo (starting at $1,999) during its initial launch period.",
