    summary_en: "Apple has released iOS 27, iPadOS 27, and macOS 27, with major upgrades to 'Screen Time' and parental control features. These new tools are designed to help parents establish a safer digital environment for their children. The new features primarily focus on four core areas: content access, communication contacts, usage time limits, and control management. For children under 13, Apple mandates the use of 'Child Accounts.' Parents can finely configure the applications and websites children can access, and set age and content restrictions for media such as video and music. Additionally, the new 'Ask to Browse' feature allows children to request access to blocked websites from parents via Messages, similar to the 'Ask to Buy' approval mechanism. Parents can also set daily usage time limits, create usage schedules for different dates, and achieve cross-device control synchronization through the redesigned Screen Time architecture. Communication safety features have also been expanded to block gory or violent content in shared images and videos. All devices must run version 27 software to utilize these new features.",
