    title_en: "Android 17 QPR1 Security Update Released: Multiple Pixel Models Patch 115 Vulnerabilities",
    summary_en: "Google has released the Android 17 QPR1 update, which includes security patches for September 2026. This update has begun rolling out to multiple devices, including the Pixel 6 through Pixel 11 series. The update addresses a total of 115 security issues, in addition to 85 patches covering the September 5, 2026 patches. The scope of the patches is broad, covering multiple core components such as applications, Bluetooth, camera, display and graphics, system framework, telephony, and user interface. Key fixes include: resolving Google application crashes under specific conditions; fixing crashes when launching gaming applications; addressing camera stability issues; improving game latency and frame rates during graphically intensive tasks; resolving system crashes that may occur during application installation, uninstallation, or updates; and fixing various interface errors related to notifications, external display connections, and system language switching. Developers should note these system-level patches to ensure device stability and security.",
