    summary_en: "Google recently announced the launch of Gemini 3.8 Live and Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking, positioning them as its 'most advanced real-time conversational models.' These new models aim to make the user's interaction with AI more intuitive and intelligent. Specifically, Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking is designed for high-complexity tasks, featuring enhanced intelligence and multi-step reasoning capabilities, applicable to complex workflows such as Gmail Live (conversational search), Docs Live (draft generation and editing), and Keep Live (note creation). This model can achieve 'simultaneous reasoning and voice output,' naturally informing the user of progress through voice prompts (e.g., 'Let me check...') while executing multi-step background tasks, thereby maintaining an uninterrupted conversational flow. Furthermore, the Gemini 3.8 Live base model possesses the ability to process visual input in real-time and can execute tools and API calls in the background, allowing users to continue chatting even while waiting for tasks to complete. In performance evaluations, Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking achieved high scores in the Speech to Speech Quality Index from Artificial Analysis and demonstrated strong performance in areas like agentic task completion. These models are expected to power the Search Live experience within AI Mode.",
