    title_en: "YouTube Login Error Fixed: TV and Gaming Console Users Can Restore Account Access",
    summary_en: "YouTube previously experienced a login bug that prevented some users from successfully logging into their accounts via TV or gaming console applications. Even when entering the correct password, users might be logged out and blocked from re-entering. This issue affected a wide range of devices, including Xbox, PlayStation consoles, smart TVs, and all streaming hardware defined by YouTube as 'living room devices.' YouTube has officially confirmed that this login bug has been fixed, announcing 'fully resolved' in a community post. According to the information, this issue was likely a server-side error rather than a client-side problem requiring an app update, meaning users do not need to update the app. This fix is expected to allow affected users to resume normal access to their Google Accounts and YouTube services.",
