    title_en: "Volvo XC60 and XC90 New Plug-in Hybrid Models Feature Increased Battery Capacity and Electric Range",
    summary_en: "Volvo has introduced new Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicle (PHEV) versions for its popular XC60 and XC90 models. The most significant upgrade is the substantial increase in the battery capacity of the electric system, which significantly boosts the vehicle's actual electric range. Compared to the 2018 model's 10.4 kWh battery pack, the new models are equipped with a larger lithium-ion battery, increasing the electric range from an initial 17 miles (27 km) to 35 miles (56 km). Furthermore, the vehicles have received visual and interior updates, including",
