    title: "KISA舉辦AI安全教育，協助企業強化產品漏洞應對能力，應對全球資安法規趨勢",
    summary: "韓國資訊安全院（KISA）於15日召開「利用人工智慧（AI）的資訊安全產品漏洞應對能力強化教育」，目標是提升資訊安全產品開發企業在AI安全威脅分析與應對方面的能力。本次教育吸引了約50名資訊安全、實體安全產品開發人員及企業安全負責人參與。課程內容涵蓋了安全領域的AI趨勢、AI Agent時代的新型安全威脅，以及利用AI進行惡意程式碼分析的案例。此外，KISA也介紹了「漏洞檢查測試實驗室」，這是KISA自7月開始運營的軟體漏洞檢查測試場，支援利用如Frontier AI模型等分析工具對產品原始碼進行漏洞分析，並可提供包含分析結果與應對措施的報告。KISA指出，隨著歐盟《網路韌性法》（CRA）等國內外對安全漏洞管理要求的強化，企業必須具備從開發階段就主動檢查和應對漏洞的能力。",
    tags: ["KISA", "AI安全", "漏洞管理", "資訊安全", "CRA", "軟體漏洞"],
    title_en: "KISA Hosts AI Security Education to Help Companies Strengthen Product Vulnerability Response, Addressing Global Cybersecurity Regulatory Trends",
    summary_en: "The Korea Internet & Security Agency (KISA) held an 'Education on Strengthening Information Security Product Vulnerability Response Capabilities Using Artificial Intelligence (AI)' on the 15th. The goal was to enhance the ability of companies developing information security products to analyze and respond to AI security threats. The training attracted approximately 50 participants, including information security and physical security product developers, and corporate security managers. The curriculum covered AI trends in the security domain, novel security threats in the era of AI Agents, and case studies on using AI for malicious code analysis. Furthermore, KISA introduced the 'Vulnerability Checking Test Lab,' a software vulnerability testing facility operational since July. This lab supports vulnerability analysis of product source code using tools like the Frontier AI model, and can provide reports containing analysis results and corresponding countermeasures. KISA pointed out that with the strengthening of domestic and international requirements for security vulnerability management, such as the EU's Cyber Resilience Act (CRA), companies must possess the capability to proactively check for and respond to vulnerabilities starting from the development phase.",
