    category: "研討活動",
    title: "CISO論壇指出AI駭客威脅與數位證據追蹤挑戰：強化日誌儲存與AI安全防護機制成關鍵",
    summary: "本次CISO論壇強調，面對日益複雜的智能網路威脅，資訊安全主管（CISO）必須保持高度警覺。在駭客攻擊的追蹤方面，警方指出由於攻擊基礎設施的國際分散性，追蹤過程存在時間差（Time Gap）。因此，能否有效追蹤攻擊者內部橫向移動的關鍵證據是「日誌」（Log）。專家建議，企業應將日誌保存期限從法定的3個月延長至至少6個月甚至1年以上，以確保在應對智能持續威脅（APT）和建立網路復原力時，能有足夠的追蹤時間。\n\n另一方面，攻擊面正由AI驅動。在DEFCON等頂級駭客大賽中，前列隊伍普遍利用AI進行攻擊，使得過去耗時數日的漏洞分析和利用程式編寫，現在可以在數分鐘內自動化完成。專家建議，應避免盲目導入AI，而是根據任務特性（如漏洞發現、UI識別、重複性作業）調整使用GPT、Claude Opus、GLM等不同模型的權重。更重要的是，必須為AI攻擊建立獨立的「安全護欄」（Safe Guardrail），以防止AI在缺乏指導的情況下，對系統進行失控的攻擊。",
    tags: ["CISO", "AI攻擊", "DEFCON", "日誌", "APT", "網路安全"],
    title_en: "CISO Forum Highlights AI Hacker Threats and Digital Evidence Tracking Challenges: Strengthening Log Retention and AI Security Mechanisms are Key",
    summary_en: "This CISO forum emphasized that Chief Information Security Officers (CISOs) must maintain high vigilance against increasingly complex intelligent network threats. Regarding hacker attack tracking, police noted that due to the international dispersion of attack infrastructure, there is a 'Time Gap' in the tracking process. Therefore, the key evidence for effectively tracking an attacker's internal lateral movement is the 'Log.' Experts recommend that companies extend log retention periods from the statutory three months to at least six months, or even one year or more, to ensure sufficient tracking time when responding to Advanced Persistent Threats (APTs) and building network resilience. Furthermore, the attack surface is now AI-driven. In top hacker competitions like DEFCON, leading teams commonly utilize AI for attacks, allowing vulnerability analysis and exploit code writing—processes that once took days—to be automated in minutes. Experts suggest avoiding the blind adoption of AI, but rather adjusting the weight of different models like GPT, Claude Opus, and GLM based on task characteristics (such as vulnerability discovery, UI identification, or repetitive tasks). Crucially, it is also necessary to establish an independent 'Safe Guardrail' for AI attacks to prevent the AI from launching uncontrolled attacks on the system without proper guidance.",
